IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc1-seat`

-- Cases for the seat layer (uc1-seat.l4): the questions of a person who claims or receives Universal Credit under the Universal
-- Credit Regulations 2013, regulations 1 and 3 to 37. Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the regulation
-- named in the comment beside it, and none was copied from the output of the question. Each assertion is written equal to the
-- value the text gives and is satisfied. The arguments follow the order of the questions' GIVEN lines in uc1-seat.l4.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The Regulations themselves (regulation 1): made 25 February 2013, in force from 29 April 2013.
-- The day before the Regulations came into force.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 in force on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2013 4 28))
-- The day they came into force.
#ASSERT `Are the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 in force on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2013 4 29)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Couples (regulation 3). Arguments of the joint-claim question: for me, then for my partner: under the qualifying age for state pension credit, not receiving education, excepted from the education condition.
-- (2)(a): I am over the qualifying age and my partner is under it.
#ASSERT `May my partner and I claim jointly although one of us is over the qualifying age or in education` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Both over the qualifying age: (2)(a) needs the other member to meet the condition.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my partner and I claim jointly although one of us is over the qualifying age or in education` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (2)(b): I am receiving education and not excepted, my partner is not receiving education.
#ASSERT `May my partner and I claim jointly although one of us is over the qualifying age or in education` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Both receiving education and neither excepted: (2)(b) needs the other member to meet the condition or be excepted.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my partner and I claim jointly although one of us is over the qualifying age or in education` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (2)(b): my partner is receiving education but is excepted.
#ASSERT `May my partner and I claim jointly although one of us is over the qualifying age or in education` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Neither fails a condition: nothing for paragraph (2) to cure.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my partner and I claim jointly although one of us is over the qualifying age or in education` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Single claim by a member of a couple (3)(3). Arguments: partner at least 18, minimum age applies, in Great Britain, a prisoner, regulation 19, section 115.
-- (3)(a): my partner is under 18 and the regulation 8 minimum age does not apply to them.
#ASSERT `May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- My partner is under 18 but the minimum age of 16 applies to them.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3)(b): my partner is not in Great Britain.
#ASSERT `May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (3)(c): my partner is a prisoner.
#ASSERT `May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (3)(d): regulation 19 bars my partner and they are not a prisoner.
#ASSERT `May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- A prisoner who is also within regulation 19 is still a prisoner under (3)(c).
#ASSERT `May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- (3)(e): section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 applies to my partner.
#ASSERT `May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Nothing applies to my partner.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3)(c): a partner on temporary release is a prisoner under regulation 2.
#ASSERT `May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A partner detained in hospital under the mental health Acts is not a prisoner, so (3)(c) does not apply, and nothing else does.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3)(d): that partner is not a prisoner, and regulation 19 bars them.
#ASSERT `May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The basis of the claim (3)(1) to (3). Arguments: member of a couple, single-claim answer, each meets all basic conditions, joint-claim answer.
-- Not a member of a couple.
#ASSERT `Do I claim as a single person or jointly with my partner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `a single claimant`
-- A member of a couple whose partner is in one of the paragraph (3) cases.
#ASSERT `Do I claim as a single person or jointly with my partner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `a single claimant who is a member of a couple`
-- A couple who each meet all the basic conditions.
#ASSERT `Do I claim as a single person or jointly with my partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `joint claimants`
-- Paragraph (2) applies to the couple.
#ASSERT `Do I claim as a single person or jointly with my partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `joint claimants`
-- A couple who do not meet the basic conditions and are in no paragraph (2) or (3) case: no basis is given (fork F-3-BASIS).
#ASSERT `Do I claim as a single person or jointly with my partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Polygamous marriages (3)(4), (5).
-- A party is married to more than one person and the marriage took place where polygamy is permitted.
#ASSERT `Is our marriage a polygamous marriage` TRUE TRUE
-- The marriage did not take place under the laws of a country which permits polygamy.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is our marriage a polygamous marriage` TRUE FALSE)
-- No party is married to more than one person.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is our marriage a polygamous marriage` FALSE TRUE)
-- Polygamous marriage, an earlier marriage subsists, and its other party lives in the household.
#ASSERT `Is the fact that my spouse and I are husband and wife disregarded` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The other party to the earlier marriage does not live in the household.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the fact that my spouse and I are husband and wife disregarded` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Not a polygamous marriage.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the fact that my spouse and I are husband and wife disregarded` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Absence from the household (3)(6). Arguments: day absence began, day it has lasted to, day it is expected to end.
-- Expected to end on the day 6 months after it began: not expected to exceed 6 months (fork F-ABS).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my partner and I stop being treated as a couple because one of us has been away` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1))
-- Expected to end the day after that: expected to exceed 6 months.
#ASSERT `Do my partner and I stop being treated as a couple because one of us has been away` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 2)
-- Has in fact lasted beyond 6 months.
#ASSERT `Do my partner and I stop being treated as a couple because one of us has been away` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 2) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 2)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Responsibility for a child or young person (regulations 4 and 4A).
-- Household: normally lives with me, qualifying young person, we live as a couple, lives with two or more non-couple people, I have the main responsibility.
-- (2): the child normally lives with me.
#ASSERT `Am I responsible for a child or young person who lives with me, apart from the exceptions` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (3): not responsible for a qualifying young person with whom I live as a couple.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I responsible for a child or young person who lives with me, apart from the exceptions` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (4): the child also lives with others who are not a couple and I do not have the main responsibility.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I responsible for a child or young person who lives with me, apart from the exceptions` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (4), (5): I have the main responsibility.
#ASSERT `Am I responsible for a child or young person who lives with me, apart from the exceptions` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- The child does not normally live with me.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I responsible for a child or young person who lives with me, apart from the exceptions` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Local authority care or prisoner: looked after, planned break, with parent, with someone with parental responsibility, placed for adoption, prisoner.
-- (6)(a): looked after by a local authority.
#ASSERT `Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Regulation 4A(1)(a): a planned short break for respite excludes the period.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- 4A(1)(b): placed with their parent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- 4A(1)(c): placed for adoption.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (6)(b): a prisoner.
#ASSERT `Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Neither looked after nor a prisoner.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (6)(a): looked after within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995.
#ASSERT `Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (6)(a): looked after within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014.
#ASSERT `Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (6)(b): detained in custody pending trial is a prisoner.
#ASSERT `Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Detained in hospital under the mental health Acts is not a prisoner.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Parental responsibility (4A)(2): nation, foster parent, section 3 Children Act 1989, Scottish responsibilities.
-- England: section 3 of the Children Act 1989.
#ASSERT `Do I have parental responsibility for the child` England England FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Wales: section 3 of the Children Act 1989.
#ASSERT `Do I have parental responsibility for the child` Wales England FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- A foster parent does not have parental responsibility for this purpose.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have parental responsibility for the child` England England TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Scotland: responsibilities or rights under the Children (Scotland) Act 1995.
#ASSERT `Do I have parental responsibility for the child` Scotland England FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Scotland: the English test is not the Scottish one.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have parental responsibility for the child` Scotland England FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Scotland: a foster carer or kinship carer with whom a child is placed under the 2009 Regulations is a foster parent, so has no parental responsibility for this purpose.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have parental responsibility for the child` Scotland Scotland TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Scotland: placed under the 2009 Regulations but not a foster carer or kinship carer: not a foster parent.
#ASSERT `Do I have parental responsibility for the child` Scotland Scotland TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Wales: a person with whom a child is placed under the 2015 Regulations is a foster parent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have parental responsibility for the child` Wales Wales TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Temporary absence of the child (4)(7): dates then absence from Great Britain, one month disregarded for regulation 11.
-- (7)(a): expected to exceed 6 months.
#ASSERT `Do I stop being responsible for a child or young person who is away from home for a time` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 8 1) FALSE FALSE
-- Abroad, but not expected to exceed one month.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I stop being responsible for a child or young person who is away from home for a time` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) TRUE FALSE)
-- (7)(b): abroad and expected to exceed one month.
#ASSERT `Do I stop being responsible for a child or young person who is away from home for a time` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 15) TRUE FALSE
-- (7)(b): unless a one month absence would be disregarded for regulation 11.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I stop being responsible for a child or young person who is away from home for a time` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 15) TRUE TRUE)
-- An absence of more than a month within Great Britain does not end responsibility.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I stop being responsible for a child or young person who is away from home for a time` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 15) FALSE FALSE)
-- Responsibility (4): answers of household, local authority, absence questions.
-- Responsible apart from the exceptions, and neither exception applies.
#ASSERT `Am I responsible for the child or young person` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Treated as nobody's responsibility by (6).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I responsible for the child or young person` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- I cease to be responsible by (7).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I responsible for the child or young person` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Not responsible in the first place.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I responsible for the child or young person` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Qualifying young person (regulation 5). Arguments: date of birth, day asked, enrolled, advanced, school or college, hours, started before 19, contract of employment, UC, ESA, JSA.
-- Aged 16, before the 1st September after the 16th birthday (1 September 2024).
#ASSERT `Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 8 31) FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- On the 1st September: 'up to, but not including'.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 9 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (1)(b): approved education of 15 hours a week extends the status.
#ASSERT `Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 9 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE 15 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Exactly 12 hours does not exceed 12.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 9 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE 12 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A course of advanced education does not extend it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 9 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE 15 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3): education by a contract of employment is not included.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 9 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE 15 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (5): receiving universal credit.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 9 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE 15 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (5): receiving an employment and support allowance.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 9 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE 15 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Aged 19, started the course before 19, before the 1st September after the 19th birthday (1 September 2027).
#ASSERT `Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 8 31) TRUE FALSE TRUE 15 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- On that 1st September.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 9 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE 15 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rounding (regulation 6(2)).
-- The daily rate for a reduction under section 26 or 27 in regulation 111 is not rounded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the rounding rule apply to my calculation` TRUE)
-- Any other calculation is.
#ASSERT `Does the rounding rule apply to my calculation` FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entitlement (regulation 7). Arguments: basic conditions met, financial conditions met, regulation 19 prevents entitlement.
-- All three of the Part's subjects satisfied.
#ASSERT `Can I be entitled to Universal Credit at all` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Regulation 19 prevents entitlement even if the other conditions are met.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be entitled to Universal Credit at all` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- A basic condition is not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be entitled to Universal Credit at all` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- A financial condition is not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be entitled to Universal Credit at all` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Minimum age (regulation 8).
-- Care leaver (8)(4). Arguments: nation, eligible or relevant child (England), under 18, looked after, still owed advice (the last three for Scotland), 3 months since 14 (Scotland), category 1 or 2 (Wales).
-- England: an eligible child or a relevant child.
#ASSERT `Am I a care leaver` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- England: the Scottish and Welsh facts do not help.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a care leaver` England FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Wales: a category 1 or category 2 young person.
#ASSERT `Am I a care leaver` Wales FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Scotland: under 18, looked after, and looked after for 3 months since 14.
#ASSERT `Am I a care leaver` Scotland FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Scotland: stopped being looked after but still owed advice and assistance.
#ASSERT `Am I a care leaver` Scotland FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Scotland: 18 or over.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a care leaver` Scotland FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Scotland: not looked after for 3 months since 14.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a care leaver` Scotland FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Confinement (8)(4).
-- Labour resulting in the birth of a living child.
#ASSERT `Does my labour count as a confinement` TRUE FALSE
-- Labour after 24 weeks resulting in the birth of a child, alive or dead.
#ASSERT `Does my labour count as a confinement` FALSE TRUE
-- Neither.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my labour count as a confinement` FALSE FALSE)
-- Pregnancy (8)(1)(f). Arguments: pregnant, first day of expected week, confined, date of confinement, day asked. 11 weeks is 77 days; 15 weeks is 105 days.
-- 77 days before the first day of the expected week.
#ASSERT `Am I within the period around a pregnancy on a given day` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 16)
-- 78 days before it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I within the period around a pregnancy on a given day` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15))
-- 105 days after the date of confinement.
#ASSERT `Am I within the period around a pregnancy on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 9 23)
-- 106 days after it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I within the period around a pregnancy on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 9 24))
-- Without parental support (8)(3). Arguments: looked after, no parent, estranged, serious risk, living away, every parent unable to support.
-- (a): no parent.
#ASSERT `Am I without parental support` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Being looked after by a local authority rules it out.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I without parental support` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (b): estranged from my parents.
#ASSERT `Am I without parental support` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (b): serious risk to my health.
#ASSERT `Am I without parental support` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (c): living away from my parents, and each is unable to support me.
#ASSERT `Am I without parental support` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- (c): a parent is able to support me.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I without parental support` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- None of the limbs.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I without parental support` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Looked after within the meaning of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 rules it out.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I without parental support` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Looked after within the meaning of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 rules it out.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I without parental support` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Minimum age is 16 (8)(1), (2). Arguments: limited capability, awaiting assessment, fit note, caring, responsible for a child, partner responsible for a child, partner meets basic conditions, pregnancy period, without parental support, care leaver.
-- (a): limited capability for work.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (b): awaiting assessment and with a fit note.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (b) needs both.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (c): regular and substantial caring responsibilities.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (c) does not apply to a care leaver.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- (d): responsible for a child.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (e): my partner is responsible for a child and meets the basic conditions.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (e) needs the partner to meet the basic conditions.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (f): pregnant or recently confined.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (f) does not apply to a care leaver.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- (g): without parental support.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- (g) does not apply to a care leaver.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- None of the cases: the minimum age is 18.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The minimum age (8)(1).
-- Within one of the cases.
#ASSERT `What is the minimum age that applies to me` TRUE EQUALS 16
-- Otherwise.
#ASSERT `What is the minimum age that applies to me` FALSE EQUALS 18
-- The age condition (8). Arguments: date of birth, day asked, minimum age is 16.
-- 16 on the day, minimum age 16.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the basic condition on age` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 6 1) TRUE
-- 16 on the day, minimum age 18.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the basic condition on age` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 6 1) FALSE)
-- The day before the 18th birthday.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the basic condition on age` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 31) FALSE)
-- The 18th birthday.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the basic condition on age` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- In Great Britain (regulations 9 to 11).
-- Right to reside (9)(2), (3), (3A). Arguments: regulation 13; reg 14 jobseeker; reg 14 family of jobseeker; reg 16(5); Appendix EU leave; Zambrano; Family Permit; family of a relevant person of Northern Ireland; would have right if EEA national; that right within (3)(a) or (b).
-- A right of none of the excluded kinds counts.
#ASSERT `Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (3)(a): a regulation 13 right does not count.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3)(b)(i): only as a jobseeker.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3)(b)(iii): only under regulation 16(5).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3)(c)(i): limited leave by virtue of Appendix EU.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3)(c)(ii): a Zambrano right.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3)(c)(iii): a Family Permit entry clearance.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3A): Appendix EU leave as a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland who would have a right if an EEA national.
#ASSERT `Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- (3A) does not apply where that right would fall within (3)(a) or (b).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Remaining limbs (9)(4)(a) to (g). Arguments: worker or self-employed, family member of one, permanent right, NI family member, NI person within (a), frontier worker, family of a frontier worker, Appendix EU leave, refugee, humanitarian protection, deported or removed to the UK.
-- (a): a worker or self-employed person.
#ASSERT `Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (b): a family member of such a person.
#ASSERT `Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (c): a permanent right to reside.
#ASSERT `Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (ca): a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland with such a person within (a).
#ASSERT `Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (ca) needs both facts.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (cb): a frontier worker.
#ASSERT `Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (cc): a family member of a frontier worker with Appendix EU leave.
#ASSERT `Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (cc) needs the leave as well.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (d): a refugee.
#ASSERT `Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (f): humanitarian protection.
#ASSERT `Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- (g): removed to the UK by compulsion of law.
#ASSERT `Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- None.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Afghanistan, Ukraine, Sudan, Israel (9)(4)(za) to (ze). Arguments: ARAP leave, ex-gratia leave, left Afghanistan, left Ukraine, left Sudan, left Israel or the region, leave granted, right of abode, no leave needed, leave outside the rules.
-- (za): leave under the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy.
#ASSERT `Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (za): leave under the ex-gratia scheme.
#ASSERT `Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (zb): left Afghanistan when its government collapsed, without other leave.
#ASSERT `Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (zb) does not apply to a person within (e), and none of the other limbs applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- (zc): left Ukraine, with leave under the immigration rules.
#ASSERT `Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (zc) needs leave, right of abode or no need for leave.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (zd): left Sudan, with a right of abode.
#ASSERT `Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (ze): left Israel or the region, not needing leave.
#ASSERT `Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Leave alone, with none of the departure facts, is not enough.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Leave outside the rules, evacuees, humanitarian routes (9)(4)(e), (zf), (zg) and (4A). Arguments: day public information issued or evacuation began, day asked, leave granted, right of abode, no leave needed, was living in the country, has left and is in Great Britain, discretionary leave, humanitarian route, leave outside the rules.
-- (e): leave outside the rules.
#ASSERT `Am I within regulation 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg)` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- (zg): a safe and legal humanitarian route.
#ASSERT `Am I within regulation 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg)` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- (zf): the last day of the 6 months from 1 March 2025 (4A).
#ASSERT `Am I within regulation 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg)` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (zf): the day after the 6 months ended.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I within regulation 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg)` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (zf) needs one of the kinds of leave.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I within regulation 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg)` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 2) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (zf): discretionary leave counts for (zf).
#ASSERT `Am I within regulation 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg)` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 2) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Treated as not in Great Britain (9)(1). Arguments: habitually resident, right to reside counts, within (za) to (ze), within (e), (zf) or (zg), within (a) to (g).
-- Habitually resident with a right to reside that counts.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as not being in Great Britain` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- No right to reside that counts.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not being in Great Britain` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Not habitually resident.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not being in Great Britain` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Within (za) to (ze): paragraph (4) takes the person out of the rule.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as not being in Great Britain` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Within (e), (zf) or (zg).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as not being in Great Britain` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Within (a) to (g).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as not being in Great Britain` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Posted overseas (10)(1). Arguments: Crown office, forces, performing duties overseas, habitually resident before posting, joint claim, partner posted, accompanying.
-- (a): a Crown servant posted overseas who was habitually resident in the UK.
#ASSERT `Do I have to be in Great Britain to claim, as a Crown servant or member of the forces posted overseas, or as their partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (a): a member of the forces posted overseas.
#ASSERT `Do I have to be in Great Britain to claim, as a Crown servant or member of the forces posted overseas, or as their partner` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Not performing the duties overseas.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have to be in Great Britain to claim, as a Crown servant or member of the forces posted overseas, or as their partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not habitually resident in the UK before the posting.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have to be in Great Britain to claim, as a Crown servant or member of the forces posted overseas, or as their partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (b): the partner of a person posted overseas, accompanying them, on a joint claim.
#ASSERT `Do I have to be in Great Britain to claim, as a Crown servant or member of the forces posted overseas, or as their partner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- (b) needs me to be accompanying them.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have to be in Great Britain to claim, as a Crown servant or member of the forces posted overseas, or as their partner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (b) is for joint claimants.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have to be in Great Britain to claim, as a Crown servant or member of the forces posted overseas, or as their partner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Absence after a death (11)(2). Arguments: death of partner or child, death of close relative, Secretary of State considers it unreasonable to return within the first month.
-- A further month for a death in the family where return in the first month is unreasonable.
#ASSERT `How many months of absence from Great Britain can be disregarded after a death` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 2
-- The same for the death of a close relative.
#ASSERT `How many months of absence from Great Britain can be disregarded after a death` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 2
-- No further month unless the Secretary of State considers it unreasonable to return.
#ASSERT `How many months of absence from Great Britain can be disregarded after a death` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1
-- No death in the family.
#ASSERT `How many months of absence from Great Britain can be disregarded after a death` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 1
-- Paragraph (4A). Arguments: present abroad at the advice, paragraphs applied then, the Secretary of State is satisfied, did not enter the country.
-- All four conditions.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 11(4A) apply to me because I was abroad when British nationals were advised to leave` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- (c): the Secretary of State is not satisfied.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 11(4A) apply to me because I was abroad when British nationals were advised to leave` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- (d): entered the country when advised to leave it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 11(4A) apply to me because I was abroad when British nationals were advised to leave` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Temporary absence (11). Arguments: began, lasted to, expected end, entitled before, death partner or child, death close relative, SoS unreasonable, treatment, convalescence, accompanying, mariner, continental shelf worker, (4A) answer.
-- (1)(b)(i): not expected to exceed one month.
#ASSERT `Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Expected to exceed one month with no other ground.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3): treatment, not expected to exceed 6 months.
#ASSERT `Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (3) fails: expected to exceed 6 months.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 8 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (4): a mariner, absence within 6 months.
#ASSERT `Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 30) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Not entitled to Universal Credit immediately before the absence began.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (2): up to a further month after a death, expected end 28 February 2025 (before 1 March).
#ASSERT `Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The day 2 months after it began: not expected to exceed 2 months (fork F-ABS).
#ASSERT `Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Expected to exceed 2 months.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 2) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (4A): applies, within 6 months.
#ASSERT `Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (4B): never beyond 6 months in total, even where (4A) applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 2) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 2) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Receiving education (regulations 12 to 16).
-- Traineeship (12)(1B). Arguments: funded as stated, first day, last day, includes training and a work experience placement, open to people aged 16 but not 25.
-- Funded, 6 months, training and placement, open to 16 to 24 year olds.
#ASSERT `Am I on a traineeship` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28) TRUE TRUE
-- Ends on the day 6 months after it began: lasts no more than 6 months (fork F-ABS).
#ASSERT `Am I on a traineeship` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE TRUE
-- Lasts more than 6 months.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I on a traineeship` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) TRUE TRUE)
-- Not funded by the Secretary of State or the Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I on a traineeship` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28) TRUE TRUE)
-- No work experience placement.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I on a traineeship` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28) FALSE TRUE)
-- Not open to people aged 16 but not 25.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I on a traineeship` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28) TRUE FALSE)
-- Relevant training scheme (12)(1B). Arguments: traineeship, skills for paid work, attended as work preparation, referred by the Secretary of State.
-- (a): a traineeship.
#ASSERT `Am I taking part in a relevant training scheme` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (b): all three limbs.
#ASSERT `Am I taking part in a relevant training scheme` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- (b)(iii) fails: not referred by the Secretary of State.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I taking part in a relevant training scheme` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (b)(ii) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I taking part in a relevant training scheme` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- (b)(i) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I taking part in a relevant training scheme` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Nothing applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I taking part in a relevant training scheme` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Advanced education (12)(3). Arguments: postgraduate, first degree, diploma of higher education, higher national diploma, standard above advanced GNVQ.
-- (3)(a)(i).
#ASSERT `Is my course a course of advanced education` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (3)(a)(ii).
#ASSERT `Is my course a course of advanced education` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (3)(a)(iii).
#ASSERT `Is my course a course of advanced education` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (3)(a)(iv).
#ASSERT `Is my course a course of advanced education` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- (3)(b).
#ASSERT `Is my course a course of advanced education` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- None of the limbs.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my course a course of advanced education` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Receiving education (12). Arguments: qualifying young person, in a relevant training scheme, full-time advanced course, other full-time course with a student loan or grant, course not compatible with any work-related requirement.
-- (1A): a qualifying young person is treated as receiving education.
#ASSERT `Am I receiving education` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (1A): unless participating in a relevant training scheme (fork F-12-SCHEME: then not receiving education).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I receiving education` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (2)(a).
#ASSERT `Am I receiving education` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (2)(b).
#ASSERT `Am I receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- (4): a course not compatible with any work-related requirement.
#ASSERT `Am I receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- No course and not a qualifying young person.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Undertaking a course on a day (13). Arguments: modular; start; last day; abandoned or dismissed; that day; retaking; first day of retake; last day of retake; vacation; first day of vacation; last day of vacation; vacation straight after the final registered module; day asked; regulation 13(4) applies.
-- (1)(a): between the start and the last day of the course.
#ASSERT `Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) FALSE
-- The day before the course starts.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) FALSE)
-- The first day.
#ASSERT `Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) FALSE
-- The last day.
#ASSERT `Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) FALSE
-- The day after the last day.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) FALSE)
-- (1)(a): the period ends on the earlier day the person finally abandons the course, so that day is in it.
#ASSERT `Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) FALSE
-- The day after the person abandoned it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 11) FALSE)
-- (4): regulation 13(4) applies on that day.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) TRUE)
-- (1)(b), (2)(b): a vacation immediately following the part counts.
#ASSERT `Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 19) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 20) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) FALSE
-- (2)(b) excepts a vacation straight after the last day of the final registered module.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 19) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 20) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) FALSE)
-- (2)(a): a period of retaking examinations or completing a module.
#ASSERT `Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 19) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) FALSE
-- The same day with no retaking: outside the part of the course.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 19) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) FALSE)
-- Paragraph (2) extends only the period in (1)(b), a modular course: a vacation after a course that is not modular is outside it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 19) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 20) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) FALSE)
-- Stopped for illness or caring (13)(4). Arguments: stopped with the establishment's consent, recovered or ceased caring, the day, resumed, the day, eligible for a grant or student loan, day asked.
-- All three conditions met within the year.
#ASSERT `Am I not regarded as undertaking my course because I stopped for illness or caring` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 10 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)
-- (c): eligible for a grant or student loan.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I not regarded as undertaking my course because I stopped for illness or caring` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 10 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1))
-- (b): recovered more than a year before the day asked about.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I not regarded as undertaking my course because I stopped for illness or caring` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 10 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1))
-- (b): the person had resumed the course.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I not regarded as undertaking my course because I stopped for illness or caring` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 10 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1))
-- The day asked about is before the person resumed.
#ASSERT `Am I not regarded as undertaking my course because I stopped for illness or caring` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 10 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)
-- (b): has not recovered or ceased caring.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I not regarded as undertaking my course because I stopped for illness or caring` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 10 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1))
-- (a): did not stop with the establishment's consent because of illness or caring.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I not regarded as undertaking my course because I stopped for illness or caring` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 10 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Exceptions to the requirement not to be receiving education (regulation 14).
-- 14(1)(a). Arguments: full-time course that is not advanced, date of birth, day asked, reached 21 while on the course, without parental support. Born 1 June 2005, so 21 on 1 June 2026.
-- Under 21 on the day before the 21st birthday.
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the education condition because I am on a full-time course, under 21 and without parental support` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 31) FALSE TRUE
-- 21 on the birthday, and did not reach it while on the course.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the education condition because I am on a full-time course, under 21 and without parental support` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE TRUE)
-- 21, and reached that age while undertaking the course.
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the education condition because I am on a full-time course, under 21 and without parental support` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE TRUE
-- Not a full-time course that is not advanced.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the education condition because I am on a full-time course, under 21 and without parental support` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE TRUE)
-- Not without parental support.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the education condition because I am on a full-time course, under 21 and without parental support` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE FALSE)
-- 14(1)(b). Arguments: entitled to a benefit, which one, found to have limited capability for work before, treated as having it before.
-- Personal independence payment and a determination before.
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the education condition because I get a disability benefit and was found to have limited capability for work` TRUE `personal independence payment` TRUE FALSE
-- Attendance allowance and treated as having limited capability for work under Schedule 8 or 9.
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the education condition because I get a disability benefit and was found to have limited capability for work` TRUE `attendance allowance` FALSE TRUE
-- Carer's allowance is not one of the listed benefits.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the education condition because I get a disability benefit and was found to have limited capability for work` TRUE `carer's allowance` TRUE TRUE)
-- Entitled, but no determination or treatment before the start.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the education condition because I get a disability benefit and was found to have limited capability for work` TRUE `disability living allowance` FALSE FALSE)
-- Not entitled to a benefit.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the education condition because I get a disability benefit and was found to have limited capability for work` FALSE `personal independence payment` TRUE TRUE)
-- 14(1)(e). Arguments: we are both receiving education, my partner is responsible for a child, my partner is a foster parent with a child placed.
-- (e)(i).
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the education condition because my partner and I are both in education and my partner looks after a child` TRUE TRUE England FALSE FALSE
-- (e)(ii).
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the education condition because my partner and I are both in education and my partner looks after a child` TRUE FALSE England TRUE FALSE
-- Neither.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the education condition because my partner and I are both in education and my partner looks after a child` TRUE FALSE England FALSE FALSE)
-- Both must be receiving education.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the education condition because my partner and I are both in education and my partner looks after a child` FALSE TRUE England FALSE FALSE)
-- Scotland: a partner with whom a child is placed but who is not a foster carer or kinship carer is not a foster parent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the education condition because my partner and I are both in education and my partner looks after a child` TRUE FALSE Scotland TRUE FALSE)
-- (e)(ii): Scotland, a foster carer or kinship carer with whom a child is placed.
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the education condition because my partner and I are both in education and my partner looks after a child` TRUE FALSE Scotland TRUE TRUE
-- 14(1). Arguments: (a), (b), responsible for a child (c), single foster parent (d), (e), reached the qualifying age (f)(i), partner has not (f)(ii).
-- (a).
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (b).
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (c): responsible for a child or qualifying young person.
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (d): a single person and a foster parent.
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (e).
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE England FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (f): I have reached the qualifying age and my partner has not.
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE England FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- (f)(ii) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE England FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (f)(i) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- No exception.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (d): a single person with whom a child is placed under the Welsh Regulations.
#ASSERT `Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE Wales TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A foster parent who is not a single person is not within (d).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Scotland: placed but not a foster carer or kinship carer is not a foster parent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE Scotland TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Claimant commitment (regulations 15 and 16).
-- 15(1), (3). Arguments: first day of the period claimed, accepted, day accepted, last day of the specified period, extended, last day of the extended period.
-- Accepted within the period: treated as accepted on the first day of the period claimed.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)
-- Accepted on the last day of the period: within it.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)
-- Accepted after the period: not covered by (1).
#ASSERT `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Within the period as extended under (3).
#ASSERT `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 21) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)
-- After the extended period.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 25) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 21) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not accepted at all.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 15(2). Arguments: the day that would be the first day of the first assessment period, accepted, day accepted, last day of the specified period.
-- Accepted within the period.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted where my award is made without a claim` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 4 5) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 14) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1)
-- Accepted after the period.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted where my award is made without a claim` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 4 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 14) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not accepted.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted where my award is made without a claim` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 14) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 15(4). Arguments: the way I accepted it, the way the Secretary of State specified.
-- The specified method.
#ASSERT `Did I accept my claimant commitment in the way the Secretary of State specified` `electronically` `electronically`
-- A different method.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I accept my claimant commitment in the way the Secretary of State specified` `by telephone` `in writing`)
-- 16. Arguments: lack of capacity (Secretary of State considers), exceptional circumstances (Secretary of State considers), terminally ill.
-- (1)(a).
#ASSERT `Do I not need to have accepted a claimant commitment` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0
-- (1)(b).
#ASSERT `Do I not need to have accepted a claimant commitment` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0
-- (2): terminally ill.
#ASSERT `Do I not need to have accepted a claimant commitment` FALSE FALSE TRUE 6
-- None of them.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I not need to have accepted a claimant commitment` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0)
-- (2): a progressive disease with death expected within 12 months is terminally ill (12 is within 12 months).
#ASSERT `Do I not need to have accepted a claimant commitment` FALSE FALSE TRUE 12
-- 13 months is not within 12 months.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I not need to have accepted a claimant commitment` FALSE FALSE TRUE 13)
-- No progressive disease: the months are not read.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I not need to have accepted a claimant commitment` FALSE FALSE FALSE 3)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Financial conditions (regulations 17 and 18).
-- The minimum is one penny.
#ASSERT `Is the amount payable to me at least the minimum` 0.01
-- Above it.
#ASSERT `Is the amount payable to me at least the minimum` 250
-- Nothing is below one penny.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the amount payable to me at least the minimum` 0)
-- Less than a penny.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the amount payable to me at least the minimum` 0.009)
-- (1)(a).
#ASSERT `What is the capital limit for my claim` `a single claimant` EQUALS 16000
-- (1)(b).
#ASSERT `What is the capital limit for my claim` `joint claimants` EQUALS 16000
-- A member of a couple who claims as a single person is a single claimant under (2).
#ASSERT `What is the capital limit for my claim` `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` EQUALS 16000
-- Capital within the limit (18). Arguments: how I claim, my capital, my partner's capital.
-- A single claimant with no partner: only their own capital counts.
#ASSERT `Is my capital within the limit` `a single claimant` 15000 5000
-- (2): the capital of the other member of the couple is included, 20,000.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my capital within the limit` `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` 15000 5000)
-- Joint claimants together hold 16,000, which does not exceed the limit (fork F-18-JOINT).
#ASSERT `Is my capital within the limit` `joint claimants` 9000 7000
-- Together 16,001 (fork F-18-JOINT).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my capital within the limit` `joint claimants` 9000 7001)
-- Capital equal to the limit does not exceed it (the heading is 'Capital limit').
#ASSERT `Is my capital within the limit` `a single claimant` 16000 0
-- Over the limit.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my capital within the limit` `a single claimant` 16000.01 0)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Restrictions on entitlement (regulation 19).
-- 19(4). Arguments: day asked, a release date has been certified, the release date, detained under section 45A or 47, section 59A, section 136.
-- (4)(a): detained under section 45A or 47 with no certified release date.
#ASSERT `Am I serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Before the certified release date.
#ASSERT `Am I serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- On the release date itself: not before it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- After the release date.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (4)(b)(i): a hospital direction, whatever the date.
#ASSERT `Am I serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- (4)(b)(ii): transfer under section 136.
#ASSERT `Am I serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Not detained under any of the provisions.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- 19(2). Arguments: day became a prisoner, day asked, entitled as a single person before with housing costs (first fact), award included housing costs, sentence expected to extend beyond 6 months.
-- (2)(a) and (b) met, within 6 months.
#ASSERT `Does the exception for the first 6 months as a prisoner apply to me` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The last day of the first 6 months (fork F-6-MONTHS).
#ASSERT `Does the exception for the first 6 months as a prisoner apply to me` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 14) TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- After the first 6 months.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the exception for the first 6 months as a prisoner apply to me` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Before the person became a prisoner.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the exception for the first 6 months as a prisoner apply to me` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 14) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Not entitled as a single person immediately before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the exception for the first 6 months as a prisoner apply to me` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- The award did not include housing costs.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the exception for the first 6 months as a prisoner apply to me` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (2)(b): the sentence is expected to extend beyond 6 months.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the exception for the first 6 months as a prisoner apply to me` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- 19(1). Arguments: religious order, prisoner, the exception in 19(2) applies, serving a sentence detained in hospital.
-- (1)(a).
#ASSERT `Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (1)(b).
#ASSERT `Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (2): a prisoner in the first 6 months who meets the exception.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (1)(c).
#ASSERT `Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The exception in (2) disapplies only (1)(b).
#ASSERT `Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- None.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (1)(b): detained in custody pending trial is a prisoner.
#ASSERT `Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (1)(b): on temporary release is a prisoner.
#ASSERT `Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Detained in hospital under the mental health Acts is not a prisoner; (1)(c) is the fourth answer.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- 19(3). Arguments: the element, a prisoner to whom (2) applies.
-- Only the housing costs element.
#ASSERT `May my award include a given element while I am a prisoner in my first 6 months` `housing costs element` TRUE
-- Any other element is excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my award include a given element while I am a prisoner in my first 6 months` `standard allowance` TRUE)
-- Any other element is excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my award include a given element while I am a prisoner in my first 6 months` `childcare costs element` TRUE)
-- (3) restricts only a prisoner to whom (2) applies.
#ASSERT `May my award include a given element while I am a prisoner in my first 6 months` `standard allowance` FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Assessment periods (regulations 21 and 21A). Arguments of the first questions: the first date of entitlement, then the number of months after it (0 is the first period).
-- 21(1), (2): same day of each month.
-- The first assessment period begins on the first date of entitlement.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) 0 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15)
-- The same day of the next month.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) 1 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 2 15)
-- A year on.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) 12 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15)
-- The 28th exists in every month.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 28) 1 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28)
-- 21(2)(a): a first date on the 31st gives the last day of each month.
-- February 2025 has 28 days.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) 1 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28)
-- March.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) 2 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 3 31)
-- April has 30 days.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) 3 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 4 30)
-- February 2024 has 29 days.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 31) 1 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29)
-- 21(2)(b): a first date on the 29th or 30th gives the 29th or 30th, except in February: the 27th or, in a leap year, the 28th.
-- February in a year that is not a leap year: the 27th.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 30) 1 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 2 27)
-- March: the 30th.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 30) 2 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 3 30)
-- A first date on the 29th: February, not a leap year, the 27th.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 29) 1 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 2 27)
-- February in a leap year: the 28th.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 29) 1 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 2 28)
-- March: the 29th.
#ASSERT `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 29) 2 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 3 29)
-- Assessment period containing a day (21(1)). Arguments: first date of entitlement, the day.
-- The period that began on 15 March.
#ASSERT `On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15)
-- The first day of a period is in it.
#ASSERT `On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15)
-- The last day of the previous period.
#ASSERT `On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 2 15)
-- Before the first date of entitlement there is no assessment period of the award.
#ASSERT `On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day begin` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 14) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The day before the next period begins.
#ASSERT `On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day end` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 4 14)
-- First date on the 31st: the next period begins on 28 February.
#ASSERT `On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day end` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 2 27)
-- The period beginning 28 February ends the day before 31 March.
#ASSERT `On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day end` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 3 30)
-- Before the first date of entitlement.
#ASSERT `On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day end` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 14) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 21(3): arguments: the new award is made to me as a single person without a claim, the old award's first date of entitlement, the last day of its last assessment period.
-- The new periods begin on the same day of each month as the old award's.
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I am a single person awarded Universal Credit without a claim` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 14) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15)
-- Paragraph (3) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I am a single person awarded Universal Credit without a claim` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 14) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 21(3A): arguments: the award is made jointly without a claim, my old award's first date and last day, my partner's old award's first date and last day.
-- Whichever of the old awards ended earlier: mine ended on 14 January.
#ASSERT `Do our assessment periods follow an earlier award when we are a couple awarded Universal Credit jointly without a claim` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 14) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 3) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 2) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15)
-- My partner's old award ended earlier, on 2 February.
#ASSERT `Do our assessment periods follow an earlier award when we are a couple awarded Universal Credit jointly without a claim` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 3) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 2) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 12 3)
-- Paragraph (3A) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Do our assessment periods follow an earlier award when we are a couple awarded Universal Credit jointly without a claim` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 14) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 3) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 2) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 21(3B): arguments: the claim is treated as made under regulation 9(8), the old award's first date and last day.
-- The new periods begin on the same day of each month as the old award's.
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when my claim is treated as made under regulation 9(8) of the Claims and Payments Regulations` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 10 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 19) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 10 20)
-- Paragraph (3B) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when my claim is treated as made under regulation 9(8) of the Claims and Payments Regulations` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 10 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 19) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 21(3C): arguments: the day I made the claim, the last day of my previous award, continued to meet the basic conditions, regulation 19 did not exclude me, first old award's first date and last day, two old awards, second old award's first date and last day.
-- The previous award ended within the 6 months before the claim.
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I claim within 6 months of its end` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 31) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 14) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15)
-- The previous award ended more than 6 months before the claim.
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I claim within 6 months of its end` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 14) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The previous award did not end before the claim.
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I claim within 6 months of its end` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 9 5) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 9 4) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3C)(b)(i): the basic conditions were not continuously met.
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I claim within 6 months of its end` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 31) FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 14) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3C)(b)(ii): excluded by regulation 19.
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I claim within 6 months of its end` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 31) TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 14) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An old award for each joint claimant: the one whose period ended earlier, the second (fork F-21-3C).
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I claim within 6 months of its end` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 31) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 14) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 9) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10)
-- The first old award's period ended earlier (fork F-21-3C).
#ASSERT `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I claim within 6 months of its end` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 31) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 14) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 9) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15)
-- 21(3D). Arguments: (3B) or (3C) applies, I meet the conditions in section 4(1)(a) and (c) and am not excluded by regulation 19 at the end of the first assessment period.
-- Paragraph (3B) or (3C) applies and the member meets the conditions by the end of the period.
#ASSERT `Does it not matter that I was below the minimum age, outside Great Britain or excluded by regulation 19 at the start of my first assessment period` TRUE TRUE
-- The member does not meet the conditions at the end of the period.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does it not matter that I was below the minimum age, outside Great Britain or excluded by regulation 19 at the start of my first assessment period` TRUE FALSE)
-- Neither (3B) nor (3C) applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does it not matter that I was below the minimum age, outside Great Britain or excluded by regulation 19 at the start of my first assessment period` FALSE TRUE)
-- Regulation 21 as a whole. Arguments: my own first date; (3) gives a cycle, its date; (3A) likewise; (3B) likewise; (3C) likewise.
-- No earlier award to follow: my own first date of entitlement.
#ASSERT `From which date do my assessment periods run` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1)
-- (3) gives the old award's cycle.
#ASSERT `From which date do my assessment periods run` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 11 15)
-- (3A) gives the cycle.
#ASSERT `From which date do my assessment periods run` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 12 3) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 12 3)
-- (3B) gives the cycle.
#ASSERT `From which date do my assessment periods run` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 10 20) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 10 20)
-- (3C) gives the cycle.
#ASSERT `From which date do my assessment periods run` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 21A: the cycle stays the same after a change in the first date of entitlement.
-- 21A(1). Arguments: the first date has been determined, it is subsequently determined to be a different date, in the Secretary of State's opinion applying 21(1) and (2) would cause unnecessary disruption.
-- All three limbs.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 21A keep my assessment period cycle the same after a change in my first date of entitlement` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- (c): the Secretary of State has no such opinion.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 21A keep my assessment period cycle the same after a change in my first date of entitlement` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (b): no later determination of a different date.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 21A keep my assessment period cycle the same after a change in my first date of entitlement` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- (a): the first date has not been determined.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 21A keep my assessment period cycle the same after a change in my first date of entitlement` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- 21A(2)(a): a period of a length the Secretary of State determines, beginning with the start date.
#ASSERT (`What are the first and last days of my first assessment period after the change` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 14))'s `first day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10)
#ASSERT (`What are the first and last days of my first assessment period after the change` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 14))'s `last day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 4 14)
-- 21A(2)(b): the text names the variables N and A but its formula is missing from the deposited text, so no amount is given (fork F-FORMULA).
#ASSERT `What amount is payable for my first assessment period after the change` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 14) 600 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 21A(2)(c): as if the day after the end of the first period were the first date of entitlement.
#ASSERT `From which date do my later assessment periods run after the change` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 14) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 4 15)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deduction of income and work allowance (regulation 22).
-- 22(2) and the table. Arguments: the award has a housing costs element, responsible for a child or qualifying young person, limited capability for work.
-- No housing costs element: the higher allowance.
#ASSERT `What is my work allowance` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 710
-- Limited capability for work: the higher allowance.
#ASSERT `What is my work allowance` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 710
-- Housing costs element: the lower allowance.
#ASSERT `What is my work allowance` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 427
-- Housing costs element and limited capability for work.
#ASSERT `What is my work allowance` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 427
-- Both.
#ASSERT `What is my work allowance` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST 427
-- (1)(b)(i): no work allowance is specified.
#ASSERT `What is my work allowance` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No work allowance is specified for this claimant.
#ASSERT `What is my work allowance` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 22(1), (3). Arguments: how I claim, my income, my partner's income.
-- A single claimant: their own income.
#ASSERT `What income of mine and my partner's is taken into account` `a single claimant` 500 300 EQUALS 500
-- Joint claimants: their combined income.
#ASSERT `What income of mine and my partner's is taken into account` `joint claimants` 500 300 EQUALS 800
-- (3): the same as if the couple were joint claimants.
#ASSERT `What income of mine and my partner's is taken into account` `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` 500 300 EQUALS 800
-- Deduction (22(1)). Arguments: unearned income, earned income, housing costs element, responsible for a child, limited capability for work.
-- No work allowance: all the unearned income (100) and 55% of the earned income (550).
#ASSERT `How much is deducted from my maximum amount for my income` 100 1000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 650
-- Higher allowance 710: 55% of 290.
#ASSERT `How much is deducted from my maximum amount for my income` 0 1000 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 159.5
-- Lower allowance 427: 50 plus 55% of 573.
#ASSERT `How much is deducted from my maximum amount for my income` 50 1000 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 365.15
-- Earned income does not exceed the work allowance: nothing is deducted for it.
#ASSERT `How much is deducted from my maximum amount for my income` 0 500 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Earned income equal to the allowance does not exceed it.
#ASSERT `How much is deducted from my maximum amount for my income` 0 710 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Amount of the award (22(1)). Arguments: maximum amount, the amount deducted.
-- The maximum amount less the amount deducted.
#ASSERT `How much Universal Credit am I awarded for an assessment period` 1000 650 EQUALS 350
-- Nothing deducted.
#ASSERT `How much Universal Credit am I awarded for an assessment period` 1228.84 0 EQUALS 1228.84
-- Regulation 22 does not floor the figure: a deduction above the maximum amount gives a negative number here. What is then paid is not stated in this regulation (finding on regulation 22 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `How much Universal Credit am I awarded for an assessment period` 400 650 EQUALS (0 MINUS 250)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 22A: a late re-claim after losing a job.
-- 22A(1), (3). Arguments: (3C) applies, not in paid work, the day I ceased paid work, the last day of the previous award, the day I made the claim, good reason, the extended number of days.
-- Ceased paid work after the previous award ended and before the 7 days ending with the claim.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE 7
-- The 7 days ending with 10 March begin on 4 March: 3 March is outside them.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 3) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE 7
-- 4 March is the first of the 7 days.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 4) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE 7)
-- Within the 7 days.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE 7)
-- Ceased paid work before the previous award ended.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE 7)
-- (3): good reason, the 7 days extended to 14 (25 February to 10 March), which include 1 March.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) TRUE 14)
-- Outside the extended 14 days.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 2 24) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) TRUE 14
-- A shorter period is not an extension: the 7 days stand.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) TRUE 5)
-- Without good reason the period is not extended.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE 14
-- (1)(b): in paid work.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE 7)
-- (1)(a): not a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE 7)
-- The period of 7 days.
#ASSERT `How many days end with the day of my claim, for regulation 22A` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE 7 EQUALS 7
-- Extended because there is good reason.
#ASSERT `How many days end with the day of my claim, for regulation 22A` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) TRUE 14 EQUALS 14
-- No good reason.
#ASSERT `How many days end with the day of my claim, for regulation 22A` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE 14 EQUALS 7
-- An extension cannot shorten the period.
#ASSERT `How many days end with the day of my claim, for regulation 22A` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) TRUE 5 EQUALS 7
-- 22A(2): N is the number of days in the period beginning with the day the claim is made and ending with the last day of the assessment period.
-- 10 to 31 March, both days counted.
#ASSERT `How many days run from my claim to the end of the assessment period` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 31) EQUALS 22
-- A claim made on the last day.
