-- The elements of an award (regulations 23 and 24).
-- 23(1). The maximum amount is made up of the elements. Arguments: standard allowance, child element, housing costs element, LCWRA element, carer element, childcare costs element.
-- Standard allowance, one child and a housing costs element: 424.90 + 303.94 + 500.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum amount of my award` 424.9 303.94 500 0 0 0 EQUALS 1228.84
-- Standard allowance, LCWRA element, carer element and childcare costs element: 338.58 + 217.26 + 209.34 + 1071.09.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum amount of my award` 338.58 0 0 217.26 209.34 1071.09 EQUALS 1836.27
-- No elements.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum amount of my award` 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 0
-- 23(2): the elements under section 12 are the LCWRA, carer and childcare costs elements.
-- (2)(a).
#ASSERT `Is an element one that section 12 of the Act includes in an award` `LCWRA element`
-- (2)(b).
#ASSERT `Is an element one that section 12 of the Act includes in an award` `carer element`
-- (2)(c).
#ASSERT `Is an element one that section 12 of the Act includes in an award` `childcare costs element`
-- Section 9, not section 12.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an element one that section 12 of the Act includes in an award` `standard allowance`)
-- Section 10.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an element one that section 12 of the Act includes in an award` `child element`)
-- Section 11.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an element one that section 12 of the Act includes in an award` `housing costs element`)
-- 24(2). Arguments: entitled to a benefit, which benefit, then entitled to the care component of DLA at the highest rate, of Scottish adult DLA at the highest rate, of child disability payment at the highest rate, the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate, of PIP at the enhanced rate, certified severely sight impaired or blind, certificate by a consultant ophthalmologist.
-- (2)(a): entitled to personal independence payment.
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` TRUE `personal independence payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the lower rate`
-- (2)(a): entitled to disability living allowance.
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` TRUE `disability living allowance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the lower rate`
-- Carer's allowance is not one of the benefits in (2)(a).
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` TRUE `carer's allowance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no additional amount`
-- Not entitled to a benefit.
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` FALSE `personal independence payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no additional amount`
-- (2)(b)(i): the care component of DLA at the highest rate, so (a) does not apply.
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` TRUE `disability living allowance` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the higher rate`
-- (2)(b)(i): the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate.
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` TRUE `child disability payment` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the higher rate`
-- (2)(b)(i): the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate.
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` TRUE `adult disability payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the higher rate`
-- (2)(b)(i): the daily living component of PIP at the enhanced rate.
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` TRUE `personal independence payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the higher rate`
-- (2)(b)(i): the care component of Scottish adult DLA at the highest rate.
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` TRUE `Scottish adult disability living allowance` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the higher rate`
-- (2)(b)(ii): blind, certified by a consultant ophthalmologist.
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` FALSE `attendance allowance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the higher rate`
-- Certified, but not by a consultant ophthalmologist: not 'blind' as regulation 2 defines it.
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` FALSE `attendance allowance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no additional amount`
-- Blind, with a lower-rate benefit: the higher rate (unless sub-paragraph (b) applies).
#ASSERT `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` TRUE `personal independence payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the higher rate`
-- 24(1), (2) and the table. Arguments: number of children and qualifying young persons, number who are disabled at the lower rate, number at the higher rate.
-- 2 x 303.94 + 164.79.
#ASSERT `How much is the child element of my award` 2 1 0 EQUALS 772.67
-- 3 x 303.94 + 164.79 + 514.71.
#ASSERT `How much is the child element of my award` 3 1 1 EQUALS 1591.32
-- One child, not disabled.
#ASSERT `How much is the child element of my award` 1 0 0 EQUALS 303.94
-- No child.
#ASSERT `How much is the child element of my award` 0 0 0 EQUALS 0

