-- Period 1, ceased in period 0.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1) FALSE `statutory sick pay`
-- (2)(a)(iii): the second period of the award, ceased in the month immediately preceding the commencement of the award (15 December to 14 January).
#ASSERT `Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 12 20) FALSE `statutory sick pay`
-- (2)(a)(iii): the first period of the award.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 12 20) FALSE `statutory sick pay`
-- Ceased before that month.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 12 10) FALSE `statutory sick pay`)
-- (iii) is for the first or second period only: this is the third.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 12 20) FALSE `statutory sick pay`)
-- (2)(b): receiving statutory sick pay.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE `statutory sick pay`
-- (2)(b): a maternity allowance.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE `maternity allowance`
-- (2)(b): statutory neonatal care pay.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE `statutory neonatal care pay`
-- Carer's allowance is not one of the payments listed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE `carer's allowance`)
-- Not receiving it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE `statutory sick pay`)
-- 32(1). Arguments: in paid work, treated as in paid work under (2), an offer of paid work due to start before the end of the next period, member of a couple, the other member in paid work, the other cannot provide childcare because of limited capability for work, caring, temporary absence.
-- (1)(a): in paid work, not a couple.
#ASSERT `Is the work condition for childcare costs met` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Treated as in paid work under (2).
#ASSERT `Is the work condition for childcare costs met` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (1)(a): an offer of paid work.
#ASSERT `Is the work condition for childcare costs met` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- None of the limbs of (1)(a).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the work condition for childcare costs met` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (1)(b): the other member is in paid work.
#ASSERT `Is the work condition for childcare costs met` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (1)(b)(i): the other member cannot provide childcare because of limited capability for work.
#ASSERT `Is the work condition for childcare costs met` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (1)(b)(ii): caring responsibilities.
#ASSERT `Is the work condition for childcare costs met` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- (1)(b)(iii): temporarily absent from the household.
#ASSERT `Is the work condition for childcare costs met` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- (1)(b): the other member is neither in paid work nor unable to provide childcare.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the work condition for childcare costs met` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (1)(a) fails although the other member is in paid work.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the work condition for childcare costs met` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- 33(1)(za), (2), (3). Arguments: first date of entitlement, I paid charges, the day I paid, the day I reported, late reporting is accepted.
-- Paid in period 0 (15 January to 14 February); reported in period 1, the period that follows.
#ASSERT `Have I paid my childcare charges and told the Secretary of State in time` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 20) FALSE
-- Reported on the last day of the period that follows (14 March).
#ASSERT `Have I paid my childcare charges and told the Secretary of State in time` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14) FALSE
-- Reported one day later.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I paid my childcare charges and told the Secretary of State in time` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) FALSE)
-- (2): late reporting accepted.
#ASSERT `Have I paid my childcare charges and told the Secretary of State in time` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15) TRUE
-- No charges paid.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I paid my childcare charges and told the Secretary of State in time` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE)
-- (3): the last day of the period that follows the period of payment.
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell the Secretary of State about my childcare charges` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 20) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14)
-- Paid on the last day of period 0.
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell the Secretary of State about my childcare charges` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 14) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 3 14)
-- Paid on the first day of period 1.
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell the Secretary of State about my childcare charges` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 15) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 4 14)
-- 33(1)(a). Arguments: a child, a qualifying young person, date of birth, I am responsible for the person, the first day of the period. Born 1 June 2009: 16 on 1 June 2025, and the 1st September following is 1 September 2025.
-- (i): a child I am responsible for.
#ASSERT `Are my childcare charges for a child or young person I am responsible for` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2015 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15)
-- (ii): a qualifying young person who has not reached the 1st September following the 16th birthday.
#ASSERT `Are my childcare charges for a child or young person I am responsible for` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2009 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 8 15)
-- After that 1st September.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my childcare charges for a child or young person I am responsible for` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2009 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 10 15))
-- Not a person for whom I am responsible.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my childcare charges for a child or young person I am responsible for` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2015 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15))
-- Neither a child nor a qualifying young person.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my childcare charges for a child or young person I am responsible for` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2015 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 15))
-- 33(1)(b). Arguments: the arrangements enable me to take up or continue paid work, I am treated as in paid work under 32(2), the arrangements enable me to maintain earlier arrangements.
-- (i).
#ASSERT `Are my childcare charges for qualifying childcare arrangements` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (ii): treated as in paid work, and the arrangements maintain those in place when I ceased work.
#ASSERT `Are my childcare charges for qualifying childcare arrangements` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Treated as in paid work, but the arrangements do not maintain earlier ones.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my childcare charges for qualifying childcare arrangements` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (ii) applies only where treated as in paid work by regulation 32(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my childcare charges for qualifying childcare arrangements` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Neither.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my childcare charges for qualifying childcare arrangements` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- 33(1). Arguments: paid and reported in time, for a child or young person I am responsible for, for qualifying arrangements.
-- (za), (a) and (b).
#ASSERT `Is the childcare costs condition met` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- (za) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the childcare costs condition met` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- (a) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the childcare costs condition met` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- (b) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the childcare costs condition met` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- 34A(1), (3). Arguments: first date of entitlement, the day paid, a day in the period for which care was provided, a day in the period in question (period 2: 15 March to 14 April).
-- (a): paid in that period for care in that period.
#ASSERT `Are my childcare charges attributable to a given assessment period` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 25) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 28)
-- (b): paid in that period for care in a previous period.
#ASSERT `Are my childcare charges attributable to a given assessment period` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 28)
-- (c): paid in the previous period for care in that period.
#ASSERT `Are my childcare charges attributable to a given assessment period` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 25) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 28)
-- (c): paid two periods before.
#ASSERT `Are my childcare charges attributable to a given assessment period` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 25) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 28)
-- Paid in a later period.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my childcare charges attributable to a given assessment period` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 25) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 28))
-- Paid more than two periods before the period of the care.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my childcare charges attributable to a given assessment period` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 25) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 28))
-- (3): the month before the award begins counts as a period, and is the previous period to period 0 for period 1.
#ASSERT `Are my childcare charges attributable to a given assessment period` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 25) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28)
-- Three periods before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my childcare charges attributable to a given assessment period` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 25) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 28))
-- 34A(2): the formula is not in the deposited text (fork F-FORMULA).
#ASSERT `How much of a childcare payment made in advance counts for an assessment period` 900 30 10 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 34(3). Arguments: out of funds provided by the Secretary of State or the Scottish or Welsh Ministers in connection with work-related activity or training, made by the Secretary of State, took up or increased paid work, required to pay before receiving the universal credit payment, less likely to continue if not taken into account.
-- Funds provided in connection with work-related activity or training.
#ASSERT `Is a payment I receive other relevant support, which is left out of account` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Not out of such funds.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a payment I receive other relevant support, which is left out of account` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Excluded: a payment by the Secretary of State where (a), (b) and (c) are all met.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a payment I receive other relevant support, which is left out of account` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (c) fails, so the exclusion does not apply.
#ASSERT `Is a payment I receive other relevant support, which is left out of account` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- (a) fails.
#ASSERT `Is a payment I receive other relevant support, which is left out of account` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- (b) fails.
#ASSERT `Is a payment I receive other relevant support, which is left out of account` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- The exclusion is for payments made by the Secretary of State only.
#ASSERT `Is a payment I receive other relevant support, which is left out of account` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 34(2). Arguments: charges attributable to the period, the amount the Secretary of State considers excessive, the amount met or reimbursed or covered by other relevant support.
-- 600 less 50 less 100.
#ASSERT `How much of my childcare charges count after amounts are left out` 600 50 100 EQUALS 450
-- Nothing left out.
#ASSERT `How much of my childcare charges count after amounts are left out` 600 0 0 EQUALS 600
-- 34(1) and the table in regulation 36. Arguments: the charges that count, the number of children. 85% of the charges, or the maximum if less.
-- 85% of 500 is 425, below 1,071.09.
#ASSERT `How much is my childcare costs element for an assessment period` 500 1 EQUALS JUST 425
-- 85% of 2,000 is 1,700, above the maximum for one child.
#ASSERT `How much is my childcare costs element for an assessment period` 2000 1 EQUALS JUST 1071.09
-- 85% of 2,000 is 1,700, below 1,836.16.
#ASSERT `How much is my childcare costs element for an assessment period` 2000 2 EQUALS JUST 1700
-- The maximum for two or more children.
#ASSERT `How much is my childcare costs element for an assessment period` 3000 2 EQUALS JUST 1836.16
-- Three children: two or more.
#ASSERT `How much is my childcare costs element for an assessment period` 3000 3 EQUALS JUST 1836.16
-- No child: the table gives no maximum.
#ASSERT `How much is my childcare costs element for an assessment period` 500 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 35(2): England. Arguments: a child or qualifying young person, registered under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006, in breach of a requirement to register, part of a school's activities, an inspected school, out of school hours, the child has reached compulsory school age, a domiciliary care provider registered with the CQC, a close relative in the child's home, the child's foster parent, by the governing body, no governing body, by those who manage the school.
-- (2)(a).
