-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The amounts of the elements (regulation 36) and run-on after a death (regulation 37).
-- 36(1): standard allowance. Arguments: how I claim, my age, my partner's age.
-- A single claimant aged under 25.
#ASSERT `What is my standard allowance for an assessment period` `a single claimant` 24 0 EQUALS 338.58
-- A single claimant aged 25 or over.
#ASSERT `What is my standard allowance for an assessment period` `a single claimant` 25 0 EQUALS 424.9
-- Joint claimants both aged under 25.
#ASSERT `What is my standard allowance for an assessment period` `joint claimants` 22 23 EQUALS 528.34
-- Joint claimants where either is aged 25 or over.
#ASSERT `What is my standard allowance for an assessment period` `joint claimants` 22 25 EQUALS 666.97
-- Where either is 25 or over: the older one is me.
#ASSERT `What is my standard allowance for an assessment period` `joint claimants` 30 20 EQUALS 666.97
-- (3): the amount for a single claimant, by my own age.
#ASSERT `What is my standard allowance for an assessment period` `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` 22 40 EQUALS 338.58
-- (3): a single claimant aged 25 or over.
#ASSERT `What is my standard allowance for an assessment period` `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` 30 20 EQUALS 424.9
-- 36(1): additional amount for a disabled child or young person.
-- The lower rate.
#ASSERT `What is the additional amount for a disabled child or young person` `the lower rate` EQUALS 164.79
-- The higher rate.
#ASSERT `What is the additional amount for a disabled child or young person` `the higher rate` EQUALS 514.71
-- No additional amount.
#ASSERT `What is the additional amount for a disabled child or young person` `no additional amount` EQUALS 0
-- 36(1): LCWRA element. Arguments: pre-2026 claimant, severe conditions criteria claimant, terminally ill.
-- Other than a pre-2026 claimant, a severe conditions criteria claimant or a claimant who is terminally ill.
#ASSERT `What is my LCWRA element for an assessment period` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS 217.26
-- A pre-2026 claimant.
#ASSERT `What is my LCWRA element for an assessment period` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS 429.8
-- A severe conditions criteria claimant.
#ASSERT `What is my LCWRA element for an assessment period` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS 429.8
-- Terminally ill.
#ASSERT `What is my LCWRA element for an assessment period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 6 EQUALS 429.8
-- Terminally ill: death expected within 12 months.
#ASSERT `What is my LCWRA element for an assessment period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 12 EQUALS 429.8
-- Death expected in 13 months: not terminally ill.
#ASSERT `What is my LCWRA element for an assessment period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 13 EQUALS 217.26
-- 36(1): maximum childcare costs element.
-- No child.
#ASSERT `What is the most my childcare costs element can be` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- One child.
#ASSERT `What is the most my childcare costs element can be` 1 EQUALS JUST 1071.09
-- Two children.
#ASSERT `What is the most my childcare costs element can be` 2 EQUALS JUST 1836.16
-- Two or more.
#ASSERT `What is the most my childcare costs element can be` 3 EQUALS JUST 1836.16
-- 37. Arguments: who has died, first date of entitlement, the day of the death, a day in the period for which the maximum amount is calculated. Death on 20 March 2025, in the period 15 March to 14 April; the period of the death and the following two are 15 March to 14 June.
-- (a): the period in which the death occurs.
#ASSERT `Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died` `one member of the couple, in the case of a joint award` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 25)
-- The first following period.
#ASSERT `Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died` `one member of the couple, in the case of a joint award` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 20)
-- The second following period.
#ASSERT `Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died` `one member of the couple, in the case of a joint award` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 5 20)
-- The third period after: the run-on has ended.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died` `one member of the couple, in the case of a joint award` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 20))
-- A period before the death.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died` `one member of the couple, in the case of a joint award` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10))
-- (b).
#ASSERT `Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died` `a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant was responsible` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 20)
-- (c).
#ASSERT `Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died` `a severely disabled person for whom a claimant had regular and substantial caring responsibilities` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 20)
-- (d).
#ASSERT `Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died` `a non-dependant within the meaning of paragraph 9(2) of Schedule 4` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 20)
-- Anyone else: the regulation names only four kinds of person.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died` `another person` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 20))
